menu "ESP-Playlist"
    config ESP_PLAYLIST_COMPACT_THRESHOLD
        int "Deleted value bytes percentage triggering catalog compaction (0 disables)"
        default 25
        range 0 100
        help
            After a successful deletion, reclaim unused value data when its share
            reaches this percentage. Media IDs and row slots remain stable;
            0 disables automatic compaction.

    config ESP_PLAYLIST_NAME_MAX
        int "Maximum playlist name length (bytes, including NUL)"
        default 64
        range 16 256
        help
            Size of playlist_name in esp_playlist_info_t. Changing this value
            changes the component ABI; rebuild all dependent components after
            modification.

    config ESP_PLAYLIST_MEDIA_NAME_MAX
        int "Maximum media display name length (bytes, including NUL)"
        default 128
        range 32 512
        help
            Size of media_name in esp_playlist_info_t. Strings longer than this
            are truncated when calling curr/next/prev/get_info.

    config ESP_PLAYLIST_URL_MAX
        int "Maximum media URL length (bytes, including NUL)"
        default 128
        range 32 1024
        help
            Size of media_url in esp_playlist_info_t. Long SD card paths or HTTP
            URLs may need a larger value; each esp_playlist_info_t on the stack
            grows by (new - old) bytes for this field.

    config ESP_PLAYLIST_FILE_SIZE_MAX
        int "Maximum playlist JSON file size accepted by esp_playlist_load (bytes)"
        default 262144
        range 1024 4194304
        help
            esp_playlist_load() refuses files larger than this instead of
            allocating the whole file plus its cJSON tree in RAM, and
            esp_playlist_save() returns ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE instead of writing
            a file that load would refuse.
endmenu
